>> title: Arroz con Pollo
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: rice, chicken, sofrito, one-pot, latin, dinner
>> counters: One Pot
>> aka: chicken and rice, arroz con pollo a la latina, yellow rice with chicken, pollo con arroz
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr 15 min
>> slack: narrow — once the lid goes on it stays on, because rice stirred while it absorbs turns to paste at the bottom and stays hard on top, and neither half can be fixed afterwards; twenty-two minutes and ten of resting is the whole of it
>> step.1: The rice cooks in the liquid the bird gave up, which is the move this whole section is built on. Skin the browning off into the pot, build the sofrito in that fat, and the rice takes its colour and its salt from what is already there rather than from anything added later.
>> step.2: brown 10 min, skin side down
>> step.3: sweat the sofrito 8 min
>> step.4: toast the rice 2 min
>> step.5: simmer covered 22 min, lid shut
>> step.6: rest 10 min, fold in
>> step.7: Once the lid goes on, leave it. Rice that is stirred while it absorbs turns to paste at the bottom and stays hard on top, and the crust that forms under it is a good thing rather than a burnt one — scrape it up when you fold, and it goes through the whole pot.

The rice cooks in the liquid the bird gave up, which is the move this whole section is built on. Skin the browning off into the pot, build the sofrito in that fat, and the rice takes its colour and its salt from what is already there rather than from anything added later.

Brown @bone-in chicken thighs{3%lb}(1.4 kg; skin on), @kosher salt{2%tsp}, @ground cumin{1%tsp} in @olive oil{2%Tbs} in a #Dutch oven{} for ~brown{10%min}.

Soften @&(~1)browned chicken{} with @yellow onion{1%large}(diced), @green bell pepper{1%large}(diced), @garlic{5%cloves}(minced), @plum tomatoes{2}(grated), @cilantro stems{1/4%cup}(chopped) for ~saute{8%min}.

Toast @&(~1)sofrito{} with @long-grain white rice{2%cups}(400 g), @achiote powder{1%tsp}, @dried oregano{1%tsp}, @bay leaf{1} for ~toast{2%min}.

Simmer @&(~1)rice{} covered with @chicken stock{3 1/2%cups}(830 mL) for ~simmer{22%min}, undisturbed.

Rest @&(~1)arroz con pollo{} off the heat for ~rest{10%min}, then fold in @frozen peas{1%cup}(150 g), @pimiento-stuffed olives{1/3%cup}(55 g; sliced), @cilantro leaves{1/4%cup}.

Once the lid goes on, leave it. Rice that is stirred while it absorbs turns to paste at the bottom and stays hard on top, and the crust that forms under it is a good thing rather than a burnt one — scrape it up when you fold, and it goes through the whole pot.
